  "headline": "Four channels put downloaded bytes on this machine and later load or execute them. Not one verifies a digest. The single length check in the tree is written if let Some(expected) = total, so it is skipped in exactly the case it exists for — and \"installed\" is defined everywhere as is_file(), which is a claim about the filesystem, not about the file.",
  "oneWay": "Treat every declared property of a downloaded artifact — its length, its format, its architecture, its identity — as a claim by the party that sent it, and check each claim against something that party does not control. Then make \"installed\" a statement about bytes, not about paths. In order:",
  "deviations": [
    "7.A — P0: an installer is downloaded without verification and executed, once with sudo",
    "7.B — P1: the one truncation check is disabled by a missing header",
    "7.C — P1: the whisper installer pins an x64 asset on a host that is not x64",
    "7.D — P1: archives extract into the live directory, so a failed install leaves a resolvable one",
    "7.E — P2: the ml download channel has none of the app's download machinery",
    "7.F — P2: no download in the model/sidecar stack can be cancelled",
    "7.G — Checked and cleared, and worth copying"
